menu "AIWatchOS Weather"

config AIWATCHOS_WEATHER_ENABLE
    bool "Enable Open-Meteo weather fetch"
    default y
    help
        Starts the weather service task: current conditions for the
        configured location are fetched from Open-Meteo (no API key)
        over HTTPS and shown by the weather app. With WiFi unconfigured
        the service stays idle and the app shows its NO DATA YET state.

config AIWATCHOS_WEATHER_LAT
    string "Latitude (decimal degrees)"
    default "39.864"
    help
        Default location is Huber Heights, Ohio. Any decimal latitude,
        e.g. "39.864". Used verbatim in the Open-Meteo query.

config AIWATCHOS_WEATHER_LON
    string "Longitude (decimal degrees)"
    default "-84.132"
    help
        Any decimal longitude, e.g. "-84.132" (west is negative).

config AIWATCHOS_WEATHER_REFRESH_MIN
    int "Refresh interval (minutes)"
    range 5 240
    default 30
    help
        How often the service refetches while WiFi is configured. The
        weather app also requests a refresh when opened with stale (or
        no) data, and marks readings older than one interval as STALE.

endmenu
